                <pb facs="0494" n="485" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg485"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.51 Public Works Debt/141: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Beaulac</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-10-19T13:00:00-05:00">October 19, 1938—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>117. For the Under Secretary. I carefully reviewed with the Secretary of State
                    this morning our policy as set forth in your telegram 74, October 6, noon, and
                    in your personal letter to me of October 13. Doctor Remos took careful notes and
                    expressed the wish that I see the President and outline our policy once more to
                    him. The only interpretation I can reach is that again there has been a
                    misunderstanding of our attitude on the part of the officials of this
                    Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaulac</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
